How light should be handled in Nethack 3.1
==========================================

There are lit and unlit rooms, all corridors are unlit.
If the player is not carrying any sources of light, he can see one square
in every direction. But if he does carry a light source (lamp, torch), he
can see TWO squares in every direction:

	#JZ@/			-------------
	    #-----		|   ..@..   |
	    O+   |		|   .....   |
	     |   |		|   .....   -###
	     -----		|           |  #####
				-------------

Torches can burn 200-400 turns. They are lit with wands of fire (a dragon!) or
flintstones. You can NOT easily 'turn off' a torch; you need water or a wand
of cold. Note that a potion of water is not enough! Of course torches can
be wielded as weapons.

Flintstones can be found among ordinary stones. They might not work every
time, but can be enchanced and they become tinderboxes. Tinderboxes work
always. Also using a flintstone takes more time.

Lamps can also burn 200-400 turns. They are very scarce in the dungeon, but
can be applied and thus be turned off and on. Lamps can't be wielded and
you cannot try to burn anything (doors!) with them. Lamps can be filled
with potions of oil.

Potions of oil can also be used as weapons. When you light one with a tinderbox
it will continue to burn 2-4 turns and after that it will explode! (Where are
the grenade patches..:)

When torches or lamps run low on turns left, they only light one square in
every direction, thus no longer being useful..

I don't know about you guys, but I think this is a great idea! (Though it has 
been proposed previously, if I'm not much mistaken..)

Another thing. Why can't the player see through a doorway into a room?
(The answer of course is: hard to implement.)
But still, it would be nice to see into an unlit room (with torch) like this:

	    -----
	 ##@|   |
	   #..  |
	    |.  |
	    |   |
	    -----

And into a lit one:

	    -----	-------
	 ##@|   |	|.... |
	   #..  |	|.....|
	    |.. |	|......@######
	    |#..|	|.....|
	    -----	-------

It shouldn't be too difficult to implement torches and lamps, but the last
part (seeing through open doors) might be a more difficult task. Perhaps I 
shall try this some time, who knows. (Do not count on me to do anything.. I'm
a little busy right now.) We'll see about that when patchlevel 6
is ready and shipped. Meanwhile, how about it? (And yes, when will patch 6
be ready? :)
